@startuml gvisor_architecture
title Container Runtime Comparison: Docker (runc) vs gVisor

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

' ==================== ECOSYSTEM ====================
package "Container Ecosystem" as ecosystem #Azure {
    rectangle "Container Engine\nDocker, Podman, containerd" as engine

    rectangle "OCI Runtime" as runtime {
        rectangle "**runc**\n(default)" as runc #FFB6C1
        rectangle "**gVisor**\n(runsc)" as gvisor #90EE90
        rectangle "**Kata**\n(microVM)" as kata #87CEEB
    }

    engine --> runtime
}

' ==================== ARCHITECTURE COMPARISON ====================
package "Docker (runc)" as docker_arch #FFB6C1 {
    rectangle "Application" as app1
    rectangle "libc" as libc1
    rectangle "syscall" as sys1
    rectangle "**Host Kernel**\n(shared, ~400 syscalls)" as kernel1 #FF6B6B

    app1 -down-> libc1
    libc1 -down-> sys1
    sys1 -down-> kernel1
}

package "gVisor (runsc)" as gvisor_arch #90EE90 {
    rectangle "Application" as app2
    rectangle "libc" as libc2
    rectangle "syscall" as sys2
    rectangle "**Sentry**\n(user-space kernel)\n~200 syscalls" as sentry #98FB98
    rectangle "Host Kernel\n(only 68 syscalls)" as kernel2

    app2 -down-> libc2
    libc2 -down-> sys2
    sys2 -down-> sentry
    sentry -down-> kernel2 : filtered
}

' ==================== COMPARISON TABLE ====================
note bottom of docker_arch
  | Feature | Value |
  | Isolation | namespaces + cgroups |
  | Syscalls | Direct to kernel |
  | Attack Surface | Large (~400 syscalls) |
  | Performance | Native |
  | Compatibility | Full |
end note

note bottom of gvisor_arch
  | Feature | Value |
  | Isolation | User-space kernel |
  | Syscalls | Intercepted by Sentry |
  | Attack Surface | Small (~68 syscalls) |
  | Performance | ~10-30% overhead |
  | Compatibility | Partial |
end note

' ==================== ATTACK SURFACE ====================
note as attack_surface
  **Attack Surface Comparison**

  runc:        ████████████████████ (400 syscalls)
  gVisor:      ████ (68 syscalls to host)
  Firecracker: █ (hardware boundary)
end note

' ==================== USE CASES ====================
note as use_cases
  **Recommended Use Cases**

  | Scenario | Recommendation |
  | General apps | Docker (runc) |
  | **Untrusted code** | **gVisor** |
  | Max performance | Docker (runc) |
  | Max security | Firecracker |
end note

' ==================== LAYOUT ====================
docker_arch -[hidden]right- gvisor_arch
attack_surface -[hidden]down- use_cases

@enduml
